=== meta ===
bypass: 107
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: a weakened assertion in a pytest file kept under tests/golden/ is judged as a test beside its snapshot role
origin: issue #219 E1 (ruled 219.Q1 and 219.Q2, 2026-10-04) - v0.6.0 reported only the snapshot rule's EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED high, a message about a stored expectation; the same edit in tests/test_x.py reports ASSERT_WEAKENED high
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total():
    return 78.75
=== before: tests/golden/test_x.py ===
from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total() == 78.75


def test_other():
    assert total() == 78.75
=== after: tests/golden/test_x.py ===
from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total()


def test_other():
    assert total() == 78.75
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "ASSERT_WEAKENED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"], "unit": "test_total"}, {"rule": "EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"], "path": "tests/golden/test_x.py"}]
